Package: mica-podman
Version: 5.8.6-2
X-Mica-Source-Date-Epoch: 1786640584
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: mica-system, nftables, libc6 (>= 2.39), libcap2 (>= 1:2.10), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2), libglib2.0-0t64 (>= 2.76.0), libjson-c5 (>= 0.15), libseccomp2 (>= 2.6.0), libsubid5 (>= 1:4.16.0), libsystemd0 (>= 246)
Description: Mica OS container engine
 podman and quadlet 5.8.6, crun 1.29.1, conmon 2.2.1, netavark and
 aardvark-dns 2.1.0 and catatonit 0.2.1, built from pinned upstream source,
 with the Quadlet system generator, the /etc/containers configuration and the
 Quadlet unit directory mount. /usr/bin/docker is an alias of podman; there is
 no Docker daemon or socket.
 .
 No unit is enabled: mica-core enables etc-containers-systemd.mount from the
 container.enabled setting. netavark execs nft, and podman dlopens libsystemd
 for journald logging, so both are declared explicitly. mica-system provides
 the /mica/containers and state mounts the configuration uses.
